SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Amsterdam: PhD\, Protest and Political Spee
 ch in the Nordics 1930-1970 (Sound of Disagreement)
DESCRIPTION:Fully funded four-year PhD position within 'The Sound of Disagr
 eement: Embodied Histories of Political Speech 1800-present'\, an interdis
 ciplinary project on how political groups have argued in public and how di
 sagreement sounds. This sub-project covers Nordic labour movements and the
  articulation of protest from roughly 1930 to 1970\, explicitly working on
  the sonic practices of political debate and the mediatization of protest\
 , so it suits researchers with a sound studies\, media studies or oral his
 tory angle as much as historians. REQUIREMENTS: a master's degree in Histo
 ry\, European Studies\, Media Studies\, Nordic Studies or a related discip
 line\; fluency in Danish\, Finnish\, Norwegian or Swedish depending on the
  chosen case study\; professional English\; archival research skills\; and
  a collaborative disposition. Apply via the AcademicTransfer posting (vaca
 ncy number 15290) with a motivation letter\, CV and research statement. De
 adline 20 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: University of Amsterdam (UvA)\, Fa
 culty of Humanities\, Department of European Studies\nLocation: Amsterdam\
 , Netherlands (Kloveniersburgwal 48)\nAward: EUR 3\,059 to 3\,881 gross pe
 r month at 38 hours per week\, on the Dutch university PhD scale\, plus 8 
 percent holiday allowance and 8.3 percent year-end bonus. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: 48 months full-time (16-month initial contract\, extended b
 y 32 months after a positive evaluation)\; preferred start 1 January 2027\
 n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362349/phd-position-on-p
 rotest-and-political-speech-in-the-nordics-1930-1970/?utm_source=artificia
